[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2847170550","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105887#issuecomment-2847170550","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105887","id":2847170550,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ptF_2","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-02T13:11:11Z","updated_at":"2025-05-02T13:11:11Z","body":"> I guess this means the functions are also declared in global scope, not just in std::?\r\nThis is curious, but if it works, it works!\r\n\r\nIt's *possible* that could be chalked up to C Header overlap with third-party includes in some cases, but ultimately no other header has the same `std::` \"requirement\" like `cmath` did. Even in that case, msvc still had global namespace math functions, so we'll keep an eye on this either way\r\n\r\nThere's a few ways to \"enforce\" `std::` functions, but those are hackier so they'd necessitate a special build argument. Well out of this PR's scope though, and not even high-priority at that, so I digress","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reaction